# Korobeiniki, the Russian folk melody (repertoire plan: korobeiniki). A new arrangement of the
# folk tune only: its eight bars, played twice, in first position (finger = fret) with one short
# shift up string 1 in bar 5: finger 4 reaches the high A at fret 5 with the hand one fret higher,
# finger 2 takes G, then finger 1 comes back to F. Bar 5 starts on the beat, as folk-song books print it.
# The strum track plays the backing chords Am, E7 and Dm, one downstrum per beat.
title: Korobeiniki
id: korobeiniki
composer: Traditional Russian
source: Russian folk melody, printed c. 1898 (sung to Nekrasov's poem of 1861; played here without words); arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: melody, minor key, russian, folk
tempo: 100
time: 4/4
key: Am

track: Melody
role: lead
